The genealogy of Jesus Christ (Luke 3:23-38)
This is the genealogy of Jesus Christ the son of David, the son of Abraham:
Abraham had Isaac. And Isaac had Jacob. And Jacob had Judah and his brothers.
Judah had Perez and Zerah by Tamar. And Perez had Hezron. And Hezron had Ram.
And Aram begot Aminadab; and Aminadab begot Nahshon; and Nahshon begot Salmon.
Salmon fathered Boaz by Rahab; Boaz fathered Obed by Ruth; Obed fathered Jesse.
Wesi brought King David. After that, David got Solomon from the wife he had taken from Uriah.
Solomon had Rehoboam. And Rehoboam had Abijah. And Abijah had Asa.
Asa brought Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat brought Joram. Joram brought Uzziah.
Uzziah had Jotham; Jotham had Ahaz; Ahaz had Hezekiah.
Hezekiah brought Menasheh. And Menasheh brought Amon. And Amon brought Josiah.
Josiah brought Jehoiachin and his brothers who were exiled Jews in Babylon.
After their exile in Babylon was over, Jehoiachin had his son Shealtiel, who then had Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel brought Abihud. And Abihud brought Eliakim. And Eliakim brought Azor.
And Azor begot Sadoc. And Sadoc begot Achim. And Achim begot Eliud.
And Eliud begot Eleazar; and Eleazar begot Matthan; and Matthan begot Jacob.
Jacob brought Joseph to Mary who gave birth to Jesus whom they call Christ.
And thus we find fourteen generations from Abraham to David, fourteen generations from David until the exile in Babylon, and fourteen generations from when they were exiled in Babylon until Christ came. The birth of Jesus Christ (Luke 2:1-7)
This is how Jesus Christ was born: When Mary his mother was engaged to a man named Joseph, before they were married, she became pregnant through the power of the Holy Spirit.
Youssef's fiancé decided to leave her without exposing her, for his own sake he was a man who feared God.
While he was still thinking about it, an angel from God appeared to him in a dream and said, "Joseph son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary home as your wife, because what is conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
And when you have a child, name him Jesus, for his sake he will save his people from their sins."
And all this is about to happen according to what God said through His prophet when He said:
Isaiah 7:14: The young woman will become pregnant and give birth to a son. You shall name him Immanuel. (Which means "God is with us")
And when Joseph woke up from sleep, he did what the angel of the Lord had told him to do, and took his wife home.
But he did not sleep with her until she gave birth to the child; and he named him Jesus.
The wise men
When Jesus was born in Bethlehem in Judea, during the time when Herod was king, Magi from the east came to Jerusalem.
They said, "Where is he who was born king of the Jews? For we saw his star at its rising and have come to do him homage."
When King Herod heard this, he was disturbed, and all Jerusalem with him.
And when the chief priests and scribes heard this, they asked him where he was born.
They answered him, "In Bethlehem of Judea; for this is what has been written by the prophet:"
But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, though you are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come for me one who will be ruler over Israel, whose origins are from of old, from ancient times.
Herod cried to the wise men without anyone hearing him and asked them about the time when the star appeared.
And after that he sent them to Bethlehem and said to them: "Go and look for the child. When you find him, come back and tell me so I can go worship him too."
After hearing what the king said, they went away. And while they were on their way, behold, the star that they had seen when it rose again went before them until it came to rest over the place where the child was.
And when they saw the star, they were overjoyed.
They entered the house and found the child with his mother Mary. They fell down before him in worship, opened their treasure chests and offered him gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
And God warned them in their dream not to go back to Herod, but instead take another route home. The escape to Egypt
After the wise men left, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream and said, "Get up! Take the child and his mother and escape to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you, because Herod is going to search for the child to kill him."
Youssef got up, shook his baby boy, and left for Egypt at night.
He was 11:1; he died at age 4:22 and lived there until Herod's death. Then what the Lord said through the prophet came true: "Out of Egypt I called my son." The killing of children in Bethlehem
When King Herod saw that he had been fooled by the wise men, he was furious and ordered the massacre of all boys two years old and under in Bethlehem and its surrounding regions, according to the time frame given to him by the wise men.
Bro, what happened is exactly what Prophet Jeremiah said:
Jeremiah 31:15 "In Ramah there was heard a cry, wailing and loud lamentation; Rachel weeping for her children, refusing to be comforted because they are no more." Return from Egypt to Nazareth
When Herod died, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream and said, "Get up! Take the child and his mother back to Israel."
They said, "Get up! Take the boy and his mother and go back to Israel, because those who wanted to kill him have died."
He got up, shook his child and wife, and went back to Israel.
But when Archelaus heard about it, he was afraid that they might go to him too; so he sent for them in secret and told them not to do this thing, saying, "Go home again."
He went to a city called Nazareth and settled there so that what was said through the prophets might be fulfilled: "He will be called a Nazarene."
