Jesus came from Galilee to John at the Jordan to be baptized by him.
But John wouldn't let him get away with that but said to him, "It is I who need to be baptized by you, and do you come to me?"
But Jesus answered him, "Let this cup pass from me; nevertheless, not my will but yours be done." And so John agreed.
And when Jesus was baptized, he came up from the water. At that moment heaven was opened, and he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove and lighting on him.
And a voice came from heaven saying, "This is my beloved Son, with whom I am well pleased."
Jesus was tempted by Satan (Mark 1:12-13; Luke 4:1-13)
The Holy Spirit led Jesus to the wilderness so that Satan could test him.
My brother fasted for forty days and nights until he was hungry.
The devil took him to a high mountain and showed him all the kingdoms of the world in their splendor. And he said to him, "All these I will give you if you fall down and worship me." Then Jesus said to him, "Get behind me, Satan! For it is written: 'Worship the Lord your God, and serve him only.'"
They answered him, "It is written: Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that comes from the mouth of God."
They shook their heads at him for going to the holy city, and they stood on the edge of the temple roof.
They said to him, "If you are God's Son, throw yourself down from here. For it is written in Scripture: 'He will command his angels concerning you, and they will lift you up in their hands so that you will not strike your foot against a stone.'"
They answered him, "It is also written, 'Do not put the Lord your God to the test.'"
He increased his shaking even more and placed it atop a high mountain, behind which lay all the kingdoms of this world and their glory.
They said to me, "We'll give you this knife if you get down on your knees and worship me."
